desc:
This figure illustrates out-of-distribution (OOD) detection using calibrated network confidence across four panels:  
(a) shows ID vs OOD data with class distributions and examples;  
(b) displays histograms of model confidence for unseen OOD data under different pretraining conditions, along with boxplots comparing performance without versus with random noise pretraining.  

(c) outlines the experimental setup where an ID-trained network (on CIFAR-10 images like a red car) is tested on OOD samples from SVHN;  
(d) presents ROC curves and AUROC values showing improved detection when using networks pretrained with random noise, as indicated by higher true positive rates at low false positives.
